          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: der Zins",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "der Zins — \"the interest (on money)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Die Bank zahlt nur ein Prozent Zinsen. The bank pays only one per cent interest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mostly plural: die Zinsen. In southern Germany and Austria der Zins can also mean rent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Zins is inherited from Middle High German and Old High German zins \"tax, tribute, interest\", an early borrowing from Latin cēnsus \"assessment, tax\" (EtymDB), from cēnsēre \"to assess\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
